>
>Simply put, some bits of armor would have sockets. One could put specific 
>gems in those sockets to gain various benefits or intrinsics while wearing 
>that armor. X amount of rubies in a socketed plate mail would confer fire 
>resistance. Elven mithril coats bearing dilithium crystals would increase 
>the caster's MP and reduce hunger. And so on and so on and so on.
>  
>
Some more not so serious suggestions:
1. Diamond encrusted armor would be "light"...cyrstal plate mail could 
actually become a  credible option.
2.  diamond as a hard substance would increase the protective ability of 
the armor
3.  dilithium in any conductive armor: mithril, plate, crystal plate, 
chain mail  would increase MP. Quality of the (substrate) armor would 
affect the MP given.
4. cheap glass encrusted armor would disintegrate
5. luckstones would automatically become lodestones regardless of BUC 
status if armor embedded
6. ameythst could provide confusion resistance
7. certain monsters would always be aggravated by such a display of 
gaudiness
8. stealth would be negated by gem encrusted armor

Rather than sockets,  a more Nethackish method might be:
1. apply sticky substance to armor (cream pies?)
2. apply gems to armor. Gems only stay stuck for d3 turns
3. foo proof your armor



